    "title": "English II: Communication and Academic Writing for Data Science",
    "credits": {
      "total": 4.0
    },
    "prerequisites": "NO",
    "courseType": "Basic",
    "availability": {
      "semester": 2,
      "year": 1
    },
    "description": "This course equips data science students with essential academic writing skills. Students will learn to organize ideas logically, develop coherent paragraphs, and write clear, well-structured essays that meet academic standards. Emphasis will be placed on critical thinking, precision in language, and clarity in presenting technical concepts. Through guided practice, peer review, and writing projects, students will enhance their ability to communicate data-driven insights effectively in research papers, reports, and professional documentation."
  },
